@page "/about"
<PageTitle>@L["The story — Mark’s Baseball Cards"]</PageTitle>
<section class="page-intro container-width" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">@L["A personal collection"]</p><h1>@L["Small cards."]<br /><em>@L["Lasting connections."]</em></h1><p>@L["Baseball has a way of bringing you back. A familiar player. A season you remember. A card that still deserves a place in the binder."]</p></section>
<section class="container-width about-grid section">
    <div class="about-print" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow">@L["THE COLLECTOR’S EDITION"]</span><Icon Name="baseball" Size="150" /><span class="about-print-year">1991.</span><span class="eyebrow">@L["FOR THE LOVE OF THE GAME"]</span></div>
    <div class="prose" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">@L["The collection, online"]</p><h2>@L["A checklist with"]<br /><em>@L["a place of its own."]</em></h2><p>@L["Mark’s Baseball Cards brings a personal 1991 Topps checklist online. It keeps the little details organized: the card number, the player, the filing sets, the doubles and the notes that make a collection yours."]</p><p>@L["You can explore the original records without signing in. The marketplace is where cards selected for sale appear, with live prices and availability. Behind the scenes, staff can maintain the inventory and follow its activity."]</p><a class="button button-primary" href="collection">@L["Take a look around"] <Icon Name="arrow" /></a></div>
</section>
<section id="collection-notes" class="section container-width collection-notes">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@L["Clear details matter"]</p><h2>@L["Know the"] <em>@L["collection."]</em></h2></div></div>
    <div class="notes-grid">
        <article><span class="note-index">01</span><h3>@L["The original archive"]</h3><p>@L["The public collection contains 64 records from the project’s original 1991 Topps checklist. It is a historical snapshot; it does not claim to be the complete Topps set or today’s sale inventory."]</p></article>
        <article><span class="note-index">02</span><h3>@L["Artwork, clearly labeled"]</h3><p>@L["Our record covers are illustrations, not photographs, scans, grading certificates or reproductions of the cards. They give the archive a visual language without suggesting a condition we haven’t verified."]</p></article>
        <article><span class="note-index">03</span><h3>@L["The details as recorded"]</h3><p>@L["Player names, card numbers, and the rookie and Royals markers are preserved from the original checklist. These markers are collector annotations, not independently certified classifications."]</p></article>
        <article><span class="note-index">04</span><h3>@L["Live marketplace listings"]</h3><p>@L["Prices, availability, condition and listing notes come from the live inventory and are supplied by the seller. Check these details before checkout. No sale, shipping time, refund policy or professional grade is implied by an archive record."]</p></article>
    </div>
</section>
<section class="container-width about-cta"><p class="eyebrow">@L["Every collection starts somewhere"]</p><h2>@L["Find your next"]<br /><em>@L["familiar name."]</em></h2><a class="button button-primary" href="collection">@L["Explore the collection"] <Icon Name="up-right" /></a></section>
